# Evidence Retention Policy — <%= projectName %>

This document defines how task-completion evidence is stored, rotated, and pruned.

## Retention Mode

**Mode:** `<%= evidenceRetention.mode %>`
<% if (evidenceRetention.mode === 'local-last-N') { %>
Evidence runs are stored under `.evidence/` and the last **<%= evidenceRetention.count ?? 5 %>** runs are kept automatically.
<% } else if (evidenceRetention.mode === 'external-bucket') { %>
Evidence runs are uploaded to an external bucket: `<%= evidenceRetention.bucketUrl %>`.
Local copies are pruned after upload. Ensure bucket credentials are configured.
<% } %>

## Scripts

| Script | Purpose | When to run |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `scripts/evidence-rotate.mjs` | Automated rotation — keeps last N runs | Called by task harness after each run |
| `scripts/evidence-prune.mjs` | Manual maintenance — supports --keep-last, --keep-days, --dry-run | Run as needed by maintainer |

## Usage

```sh
# Dry-run: see what would be removed without deleting
node scripts/evidence-prune.mjs --dry-run --keep-last=10

# Prune runs older than 30 days, skip ACK prompt
node scripts/evidence-prune.mjs --keep-days=30 --yes

# Keep only last 3 runs
node scripts/evidence-prune.mjs --keep-last=3 --yes
```

## Location

Evidence runs are stored in `.evidence/run-NNNN/` directories (gitignored).
Each run directory contains the SHA-pinned output files listed in `evidence-files.json`.

## Governance

This policy is enforced by the done-evidence harness (`scripts/done-evidence.mjs`).
Runs without valid SHA pins fail the L2 gate.
